 "literal": "Glorious-wound not-received days all, among-the-wasted he-will-place, his-own days having-taken.",
 "translation": "Taking stock of his past, a warrior will count all the days he did not receive a glorious wound as wasted.",
 "modern": "ஒரு வீரன் தன் வாழ்நாட்களைக் கணக்கிட்டுப் பார்த்து, அவற்றில் போர்க்களத்தில் விழுப்புண் படாத நாட்களை எல்லாம் வீணான நாட்கள் என்று கருதுவான்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet describes the mindset of a true warrior. The word 'விழுப்புண்' refers to a glorious wound, specifically one received bravely on the front of the body in battle. The hero reviews his past ('தன் நாளை எடுத்து') to evaluate his life's worth. He considers any day that passed without earning such a noble wound as a day that slipped away uselessly ('வழுக்கினுள் வைக்கும்'). It highlights that for a warrior, a life of passive safety is a wasted life, while physical sacrifice in battle is the true measure of a day well lived.",
